From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:43:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vfio/igd: save the host OpRegion for offline inspection

The OpRegion, which carries the Video BIOS Table, is the main piece of
host-specific state that QEMU hands a guest unchanged (x-igd-opregion=on).
When iGPU passthrough works on one host and not on another, comparing the
two VBTs is often the quickest lead, and the guest may be in no state to
dump its copy.

Write the OpRegion that QEMU has just read for the guest to
/run/hypervisor/kvm/<name>/igd-opregion.bin, where <name> is -name; EVE's
tools/igpu-vbt-dump.py decodes it. No device access is added. A failure to
write the file is reported and ignored.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [EVE-specific runtime path]
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 hw/vfio/igd.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/vfio/igd.c b/hw/vfio/igd.c
index 3b15e37..903d3ab 100644
--- a/hw/vfio/igd.c
+++ b/hw/vfio/igd.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "qapi/qmp/qerror.h"
 #include "hw/core/boards.h"
 #include "hw/nvram/fw_cfg.h"
+#include "system/system.h"
 #include "pci.h"
 #include "pci-quirks.h"
 #include "trace.h"
@@ -141,6 +142,30 @@ static uint64_t igd_stolen_memory_size(int gen, uint32_t gmch)
     return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Keep a copy of the host OpRegion, VBT included, with the domain's other
+ * runtime files, so that it can be compared between hosts without capturing
+ * it inside the guest. Best effort: a failure is reported and ignored.
+ */
+static void vfio_pci_igd_opregion_save(VFIOPCIDevice *vdev, size_t size)
+{
+    const char *name = qemu_get_vm_name();
+    g_autofree char *path = NULL;
+    g_autoptr(GError) err = NULL;
+
+    if (!name) {
+        return;
+    }
+    path = g_strdup_printf("/run/hypervisor/kvm/%s/igd-opregion.bin", name);
+    if (!g_file_set_contents(path, (const char *)vdev->igd_opregion, size,
+                             &err)) {
+        warn_report("IGD: OpRegion copy not saved to %s: %s; "
+                    "passthrough is unaffected", path, err->message);
+        return;
+    }
+    info_report("IGD: OpRegion (%zu bytes) saved to %s", size, path);
+}
+
 /*
  * The OpRegion includes the Video BIOS Table, which seems important for
  * telling the driver what sort of outputs it has.  Without this, the device
@@ -165,6 +190,8 @@ static bool vfio_pci_igd_opregion_init(VFIOPCIDevice *vdev,
         return false;
     }
 
+    vfio_pci_igd_opregion_save(vdev, info->size);
+
     /*
      * Provide fw_cfg with a copy of the OpRegion which the VM firmware is to
      * allocate 32bit reserved memory for, copy these contents into, and write
